I was playing a rather lucky wizard, and after retrieving the wand of
wishing from the castle, I wanted to check out the stores. Having no
levitation, I grabbed a scroll of earth and started filling in the
first two trapdoors, so I could easily get to the middle.
Unfortunately, I accidentally ran into the next trapdoor beyond it and
fell into the valley of the dead.

I easily climbed back up, but then couldn't figure out how to get
across. After a bit of thinking, I realized I had water walking boots,
so I put them on and started walking around the side of the castle.
Upon almost reaching the other side, I met a random monster which
happened to be a succubus (didn't think about the significance until
later). Having a decent AC and facing a fairly weak monster, I walked
up to it and started hitting it with Magicbane. Unfortunately, her
seduction attack hit next turn, and she pulled off my boots.

You fall into the water! You drown. DYWYPI?

One of those things you don't think about until after it happens...

